mcpTools.description:
Resolve security identifiers (code / Chinese name / pinyin) to {market, code} pairs. MUST be called before any other data tool when you don't already have market+code.

When you need to resolve N identifiers (N indices / stocks / ETFs in one query), pass them ALL in ONE call via 'keywords' array — N parallel resolves, 1 Anthropic round trip. NEVER emit N separate search_securities calls. Legacy single 'keyword' remains supported for compatibility.

Returns: { success, data: { results: [{ keyword: "贵州茅台", hits: [{ security, name, code, market }], error? }, ...] } }.
Legacy keyword without a non-empty keywords array returns data as a hit array. Empty hits are successful; any failed keyword sets success:false while preserving other hits.
Use returned market+code for subsequent queries. NEVER construct market+code manually.

Examples:
- Legacy single: { keyword: "贵州茅台" }
- Single batch form: { keywords: ["贵州茅台"] }
- Batch:  { keywords: ["上证指数","深证成指","创业板指","沪深300","科创50"] }

Get intraday trend (分时) data. Securities market+code MUST come from search_securities.
Returns: { "USHA600519": [{ time: UnixSec, "10": price, "13": volume, "19": amount }] }
Fields: 1=时间（Unix秒） 10=最新价 13=成交量 19=成交额. Data points are at 60-second intervals.
